  _id: 025
  _keywordName: Arthur'sAutopsy
  _description: "Autopsy \u2014 Arthur Sterling, M/60\nThe decedent was discovered
    on the kitchen floor in a supine position, with significant blood pooling beneath
    the torso and head consistent with in-situ haemorrhage. Multiple stab wounds
    are present across the neck, chest, back, and abdomen, with a total of eleven
    identified entry points of varying depth suggesting repeated strikes from a single-edged
    blade. A partially severed vertebral structure at the cervical region indicates
    one wound penetrated to the spinal column, with associated neurological trauma
    consistent with temporary motor impairment prior to death. Lacerations across
    the palmar surfaces of both hands are consistent with contact with a bladed edge
    during the struggle. Time of death estimated 6:30\u20137:30 PM; body position
    and blood distribution indicate the decedent did not move significantly following
    the fatal wound."
  _icon: {fileID: 0}
  _playerNote: 
